    "outlook": "The Indian market closed marginally positive, with NIFTY 50 gaining 0.17%, primarily driven by robust FII inflows. Sectoral performance was bifurcated, seeing strong buying interest in Auto, Realty, and Financial Services, while the IT sector experienced significant selling pressure. This led to a mixed market breadth despite the overall index uptick and a low VIX at 11.8025.",
    "keyTakeaways": [
      "NIFTY 50 and SENSEX closed marginally up, supported by FII buying.",
      "Auto (+1.69%), Realty (+0.9%), and Financial Services (+0.8%) were top performing sectors.",
      "IT sector saw significant declines, with NIFTY IT down 1.69% and major IT stocks among top losers.",
      "FIIs recorded strong net buying of 3623.51cr, while DIIs were net sellers at 1864.03cr.",
      "Market breadth was almost even (30 advances / 28 declines), reflecting mixed sentiment."
    ]
